The problem is: If $(2^3)^{(2^3)} = 2^N$, what is the value of $N$?

Step 1: Simplify the left-hand side of the equation.

$(2^3)^{(2^3)}$ can be simplified using the exponent rule $(a^b)^c = a^{b \cdot c}$.

